  title: Nehru Era
  text: Jawaharlal Nehru, Prime Minister from 1947 to 1964, built democratic institutions, a mixed economy, scientific and technical institutions such as the IITs, and a foreign policy of non-alignment. The first general elections were held in 1951 and 1952.
